{"id":"leetcode-338","version":1,"status":"approved","title":"Counting Bits","summary":"For an integer n, generate an array ans of length n + 1 where each ans[i] (0 <= i <= n) represents the count of 1's in the binary representation of i.","statement":"For an integer n, generate an array ans of length n + 1 where each ans[i] (0 <= i <= n) represents the count of 1's in the binary representation of i. Avoid using built-in functions for counting bits.","constraints":["0 <= n <= 100,000.","Return counts for every integer from zero through n inclusive without calling a built-in bit-count function."],"topics":["bit-manipulation","dynamic-programming"],"prerequisites":[],"signature":{"name":"counting_bits","parameters":[{"name":"n","annotation":"int","adapter":"raw","source_parameter":null}],"returns":"list[int]","return_adapter":"raw","node_policy":"values","result_mode":"return","mutated_parameter":null,"immutable_parameters":[]},"starter_code":"def counting_bits(n: int) -> list[int]:\n    # Write your solution here.\n    pass\n","reference_solution":"def counting_bits(n):\n    answer = [0] * (n + 1)\n    for value in range(1, n + 1):\n        answer[value] = answer[value >> 1] + (value & 1)\n    return answer\n","brute_force_solution":null,"known_wrong_solutions":["def counting_bits(n):\n    answer = [0] * (n + 1)\n    for value in range(1, n):\n        answer[value] = answer[value >> 1] + (value & 1)\n    return answer\n","def counting_bits(n):\n    answer = [0] * (n + 1)\n    for value in range(1, n + 1):\n        answer[value] = answer[value >> 1] + 1\n    return answer\n"],"target_time_complexity":"O(n)","target_space_complexity":"O(n) including output","estimated_minutes":20,"rubric":{"algorithmic_insight":1,"prerequisites":1,"implementation":1,"performance_pressure":0,"edge_cases":0},"hints":["Removing the last binary digit produces a smaller integer whose count is already known.","Reuse the count for value//2 and add the last bit.","Set answer[0]=0, then answer[i]=answer[i>>1]+(i&1) for i from 1 through n.","Each result requires constant work after its smaller predecessor is available."],"editorial":"Right-shifting an integer removes its last bit. Therefore its set-bit count is the earlier count for half the value plus either zero or one for that removed bit. Fill the array in increasing order so the earlier count is always ready. Include both endpoints zero and n. Time is linear in the output length.","tests":[{"id":"lc-338-1","arguments":[2],"expected":[0,1,1],"comparator":"exact","visible":true,"explanation":"Binary representations 0,1,10 contain 0,1,1 set bits.","expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-338-2","arguments":[5],"expected":[0,1,1,2,1,2],"comparator":"exact","visible":true,"explanation":"Counts for 0 through 5 are [0,1,1,2,1,2].","expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-338-3","arguments":[0],"expected":[0],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-338-4","arguments":[1],"expected":[0,1],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-338-5","arguments":[3],"expected":[0,1,1,2],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-338-6","arguments":[4],"expected":[0,1,1,2,1],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-338-7","arguments":[6],"expected":[0,1,1,2,1,2,2],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-338-8","arguments":[7],"expected":[0,1,1,2,1,2,2,3],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-338-9","arguments":[8],"expected":[0,1,1,2,1,2,2,3,1],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-338-10","arguments":[9],"expected":[0,1,1,2,1,2,2,3,1,2],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-338-11","arguments":[15],"expected":[0,1,1,2,1,2,2,3,1,2,2,3,2,3,3,4],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-338-12","arguments":[16],"expected":[0,1,1,2,1,2,2,3,1,2,2,3,2,3,3,4,1],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-338-13","arguments":[31],"expected":[0,1,1,2,1,2,2,3,1,2,2,3,2,3,3,4,1,2,2,3,2,3,3,4,2,3,3,4,3,4,4,5],"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-338-14","arguments":[1000],"expected":[0,1,1,2,1,2,2,3,1,2,2,3,2,3,3,4,1,2,2,3,2,3,3,4,2,3,3,4,3,4,4,5,1,2,2,3,2,3,3,4,2,3,3,4,3,4,4,5,2,3,3,4,3,4,4,5,3,4,4,5,4,5,5,6,1,2,2,3,2,3,3,4,2,3,3,4,3,4,4,5,2,3,3,4,3,4,4,5,3,4,4,5,4,5,5,6,2,3,3,4,3,4,4,5,3,4,4,5,4,5,5,6,3,4,4,5,4,5,5,6,4,5,5,6,5,6,6,7,1,2,2,3,2,3,3,4,2,3,3,4,3,4,4,5,2,3,3,4,3,4,4,5,3,4,4,5,4,5,5,6,2,3,3,4,3,4,4,5,3,4,4,5,4,5,5,6,3,4,4,5,4,5,5,6,4,5,5,6,5,6,6,7,2,3,3,4,3,4,4,5,3,4,4,5,4,5,5,6,3,4,4,5,4,5,5,6,4,5,5,6,5,6,6,7,3,4,4,5,4,5,5,6,4,5,5,6,5,6,6,7,4,5,5,6,5,6,6,7,5,6,6,7,6,7,7,8,1,2,2,3,2,3,3,4,2,3,3,4,3,4,4,5,2,3,3,4,3,4,4,5,3,4,4,5,4,5,5,6,2,3,3,4,3,4,4,5,3,4,4,5,4,5,5,6,3,4,4,5,4,5,5,6,4,5,5,6,5,6,6,7,2,3,3,4,3,4,4,5,3,4,4,5,4,5,5,6,3,4,4,5,4,5,5,6,4,5,5,6,5,6,6,7,3,4,4,5,4,5,5,6,4,5,5,6,5,6,6,7,4,5,5,6,5,6,6,7,5,6,6,7,6,7,7,8,2,3,3,4,3,4,4,5,3,4,4,5,4,5,5,6,3,4,4,5,4,5,5,6,4,5,5,6,5,6,6,7,3,4,4,5,4,5,5,6,4,5,5,6,5,6,6,7,4,5,5,6,5,6,6,7,5,6,6,7,6,7,7,8,3,4,4,5,4,5,5,6,4,5,5,6,5,6,6,7,4,5,5,6,5,6,6,7,5,6,6,7,6,7,7,8,4,5,5,6,5,6,6,7,5,6,6,7,6,7,7,8,5,6,6,7,6,7,7,8,6,7,7,8,7,8,8,9,1,2,2,3,2,3,3,4,2,3,3,4,3,4,4,5,2,3,3,4,3,4,4,5,3,4,4,5,4,5,5,6,2,3,3,4,3,4,4,5,3,4,4,5,4,5,5,6,3,4,4,5,4,5,5,6,4,5,5,6,5,6,6,7,2,3,3,4,3,4,4,5,3,4,4,5,4,5,5,6,3,4,4,5,4,5,5,6,4,5,5,6,5,6,6,7,3,4,4,5,4,5,5,6,4,5,5,6,5,6,6,7,4,5,5,6,5,6,6,7,5,6,6,7,6,7,7,8,2,3,3,4,3,4,4,5,3,4,4,5,4,5,5,6,3,4,4,5,4,5,5,6,4,5,5,6,5,6,6,7,3,4,4,5,4,5,5,6,4,5,5,6,5,6,6,7,4,5,5,6,5,6,6,7,5,6,6,7,6,7,7,8,3,4,4,5,4,5,5,6,4,5,5,6,5,6,6,7,4,5,5,6,5,6,6,7,5,6,6,7,6,7